			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Implement comprehensive keybinding system with when-clause evaluation\n\nIntroduce a full keybinding resolution pipeline across three priority layers:\n- Extension contributions (static `contributes.keybindings`)\n- Dynamic registry (`keybinding:add` / `RegisterExtensionKeybindings`)\n- User overrides (`keybindings.json` in app config dir)\n\nEach rule carries a `source` tag (`extension:<id>`, `dynamic[:<id>]`, `user`) so\nconsumers can apply source-weighted precedence. Negative commands (`-command`)\nact as unbind rules at the user layer.\n\nAdd `Environment::Utility::WhenClause` — a complete VS Code–compatible parser\nand evaluator for context-key when clauses (boolean logic, comparisons, regex\n`=~`, list membership `in`/`not in`). Mountain receives context snapshots over\nIPC; Sky owns the live context store. Wire methods `keybinding:resolve` and\n`keybinding:evaluateWhen` expose resolution and evaluation to the renderer.\n\nExtend `CommandProvider` to forward renderer-side commands\n(`workbench.action.*`, `editor.action.*`, `vscode.*`) to Sky via the\n`sky://command/execute` Tauri event so VS Code's own `CommandsRegistry`\nexecutes them. Only Mountain-private commands (`getTelemetrySenderObject`,\n`testing.clearTestResults`) remain local no-ops.\n\nAdd output channel lifecycle IPC (`output:create`, `output:replace`,\n`output:dispose`) with Sky event emission for panel registration.\n\nSearchProvider gains glob include/exclude, hidden-file, symlink, and max-results\noptions matching VS Code's `ITextSearchOptions` shape.\n\nAll dynamic keybindings are tagged with their owning extension identifier,\nenabling precise unregistration on extension deactivation via\n`RemoveKeybindingsBySource`. Resolution sorts rules by (source weight,\nwhen-clause specificity) for deterministic conflict handling.",
			"SHA": "554f2511752f00f8dc9ce2891768fc49c2207c25"
		},
